  "full_text": "Okay, so I'm going to fire up TempleOS and I want to show off a few things. Somebody doesn't know what assembly language is, so I'm just going to show them. I want to show them my code and I want to put it on my website. So I'm going to go ahead and I made a demo for converting to HTML. So I'm going to... I'm going to go to my demo, convert HTML, HTML gen, wait, to HTML. Why don't we take, I'm going to copy these. I'm going to put them into my home directory. Okay, so we don't want the text gen. Okay, now we quit. Go to my home directory and to HTML. the HTML, this is the, okay, we don't need that. Okay, so I'm going to delete that. And so we're going to invoke it and convert a document from, I'm going to go, the input document, we will input, do F4, F4, we're going to select a file. I'm going to go to my kernel and I'm going to select my scheduler. and So that's that's our input document and then we're gonna give it a output name. I'm gonna call it scheduler HTML it will put the HTML on it and this should when I press f5 Should do that now if I bail out of here, and if I look in my home directory We have scheduler dot HTML. I'm gonna go ahead and copy my scheduler dot HTML to the D drive, and then I'm going to reboot and transfer to my website. Anyway, so that's what I just did.",
